# This dialogue is triggered by clicking the bartender character.
# SPEAKER: lines set who's talking, matched to character ID (case-insensitive).
# Nodes can have multiple CHOICE blocks; REQUIRE hides a choice if the condition fails.

NODE start
  # The displayed text uses *bold* around the tavern name.
  BARTENDER: Welcome to the *Salty Dog*, stranger. What can I get you?

  # Always available: ask for rumors (demonstrates: flag, relationship, journalEntry)
  CHOICE What's the news around here?
    SET flag metBartender
    ADD relationship bartender 1
    GOTO rumors
  END

  # Always available: buy a drink (demonstrates: variable change, flag)
  CHOICE I'll have a drink.
    GOTO order_drink
  END

  # Only before accepting the quest (demonstrates: notFlag condition)
  CHOICE I'm looking for work.
    REQUIRE notFlag acceptedOddJobs
    GOTO work_intro
  END

  # Only while quest is active at "started" stage (demonstrates: questAtStage condition)
  CHOICE About that job you mentioned...
    REQUIRE questAtStage odd_jobs started
    GOTO work_followup
  END

  # Only after quest is complete (demonstrates: questAtStage condition)
  CHOICE Thanks for putting me onto that work.
    REQUIRE questAtStage odd_jobs complete
    GOTO work_done
  END

  CHOICE Never mind, just passing through.
    GOTO farewell
  END

NODE rumors
  # The displayed text nests *bold* inside cRRGGBB[color] for the old coin.
  BARTENDER: Word is there's been strange folk poking around the docks at night. And the merchant in the market square has been looking for hired help. Oh, I found this cD6A84B[*old coin*] on the floor the other day. Strange markings. You can have it.
  ADD journalEntry tavern_discovery
  ADD item old_coin
  NOTIFY Journal Updated

  CHOICE Tell me more about that.
    GOTO rumors_detail
  END

  CHOICE So, what else?
    GOTO start
  END

NODE rumors_detail
  BARTENDER: Some say they've seen lights out on the old pier after midnight. Probably smugglers, but who knows these days. Keep your wits about you.

  CHOICE Interesting. I'll keep that in mind.
    GOTO start
  END

NODE order_drink
  BARTENDER: Five gold for the house special, strongest thing this side of the river. What do you say?

  # Only if player can afford it (demonstrates: variableGreaterThan condition)
  CHOICE Sure, here's five gold.
    REQUIRE variableGreaterThan gold 4
    ADD variable gold -5
    ADD variable _drinksBought 1
    ADD variable reputation 1
    SET flag hadDrink
    ADD relationship bartender 1
    NOTIFY Bought a drink (-5 gold)
    GOTO after_drink
  END

  # Try to bluff a free drink. Rolls dice inline (demonstrates: ROLL + GOTO within one dialogue)
  CHOICE Try to talk your way to a free drink.
    GOTO bluff_attempt
  END

  # Always available as an out
  CHOICE On second thought, I'll pass.
    GOTO start
  END

NODE bluff_attempt
  # Roll happens immediately on entering this silent node. If the IF passes,
  # everything inside that IF block runs before routing to bluff_success.
  ROLL bluffRoll 1 20
  IF variableGreaterThan bluffRoll 14
    SET flag bluffedMarcus
    ADD relationship bartender 2
    GOTO bluff_success
  END
  GOTO bluff_failure

NODE bluff_success
  BARTENDER: Sure, this one's on the house.

  CHOICE Cheers!
    GOTO start
  END

NODE bluff_failure
  BARTENDER: Nope. That'll be five gold.

  CHOICE Fine. Here's five gold.
    REQUIRE variableGreaterThan gold 4
    ADD variable gold -5
    ADD variable _drinksBought 1
    ADD variable reputation 1
    SET flag hadDrink
    ADD relationship bartender 1
    NOTIFY Bought a drink (-5 gold)
    GOTO start
  END

  CHOICE Never mind then.
    GOTO start
  END

NODE after_drink
  BARTENDER: Glad you like it! Brewed it myself. Now then, anything else?

  CHOICE So, what else?
    GOTO start
  END

NODE work_intro
  BARTENDER: Well now, you look capable enough. There's a merchant over in the market square. Elena has been asking around for someone reliable. Tell her Marcus sent you.

  CHOICE Sure, I could use the coin.
    SET flag acceptedOddJobs
    SET questStage odd_jobs started
    ADD journalEntry odd_jobs_accepted
    ADD relationship bartender 2
    ADD variable reputation 5
    NOTIFY New Quest: Odd Jobs
    GOTO work_accepted
  END

  CHOICE Not right now, thanks.
    GOTO start
  END

NODE work_accepted
  BARTENDER: Good on you. Elena's fair with pay. Head to the market square when you're ready.

  CHOICE I'll head there now.
    GOTO farewell
  END

  CHOICE What exactly do they need?
    GOTO work_details
  END

NODE work_details
  BARTENDER: Something about a shipment that needs escorting. Nothing too dangerous, she says, but then, that's what they always say.

  CHOICE Got it. I'll take care of it.
    GOTO farewell
  END

NODE work_followup
  BARTENDER: Still working on that job for Elena? She's over at the market square if you haven't found her yet. Don't keep her waiting too long.

  CHOICE I'll head there now.
    GOTO farewell
  END

NODE work_done
  BARTENDER: I heard Elena's singing your praises. Good work out there. I knew you had it in you.
  ADD relationship bartender 3

  CHOICE Anytime.
    GOTO start
  END

NODE farewell
  BARTENDER: Take care out there. The streets aren't as safe as they used to be.
  END dialogue
